---
/* cssv:title Music visualizer */
/* cssv:description A music visualizer drawn from a spectrum: each record
   is a frequency band and its level. */
/* A spectrum: one record per frequency band, its center in Hz, and its
   level from 0 to 100. The level is the key column, so typed attr() reads
   it as a number and sets the length of the band's bar, and
   sibling-index() turns the band's place in the file into its angle and
   its color. Give the table the next spectrum with update() and the bars'
   transitions fill in between, so 15 updates a second move like 60 frames.
   The fourth band, 70 to 85 Hz, is where the kick drum is: it also lights
   the core. */
table {
  --cssv-key: level;
  --ring: 20cqmin;  /* where the bars start */
  --reach: 27cqmin; /* a bar at level 100 */
  --bar: 2.5cqmin;
  color: oklch(70% 0.24 300); /* what a band's bars inherit if its own hue fails */
  display: block;
  position: relative;
  aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
  container-type: size;
  overflow: hidden;
  border-radius: 14px;
  background:
    radial-gradient(circle, transparent calc(var(--ring) - 0.6cqmin), rgb(255 255 255 / 0.14) calc(var(--ring) - 0.35cqmin), transparent var(--ring)),
    repeating-radial-gradient(circle, transparent 0 7.7cqmin, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.035) 7.7cqmin 7.9cqmin),
    radial-gradient(circle, oklch(30% 0.1 305) 0, oklch(17% 0.06 285) 36%, oklch(9% 0.025 270) 72%);
}
@media (width < 640px) { table { aspect-ratio: 1; } }
colgroup, thead, td { display: none; }

/* The ring turns slowly; each band sits at its own angle on it. */
tbody { display: block; position: absolute; inset: 0; animation: turn 48s linear infinite; }
@keyframes turn { to { rotate: 1turn; } }
tbody tr {
  --level: attr(data-key type(<number>), 0);
  display: block;
  position: absolute;
  left: 50%;
  top: 50%;
  rotate: calc((sibling-index() - 0.5) / sibling-count() * 1turn);
  /* The band's color, on the row so its bars can use currentColor. A
     browser that can't work out the hue keeps the violet before it. */
  color: oklch(70% 0.24 300);
  color: oklch(70% 0.25 calc(335deg - sibling-index() * 4.6deg));
}

/* The bar, outward from the ring, and its reflection, inward. Hue runs
   from pink in the bass to cyan in the treble. */
tbody tr::before, tbody tr::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: calc(var(--bar) / -2);
  width: var(--bar);
  border-radius: var(--bar);
  transition: scale 0.13s ease-out;
}
tbody tr::before {
  bottom: var(--ring);
  height: var(--reach);
  transform-origin: 50% 100%;
  scale: 1 calc(0.04 + attr(data-key type(<number>), 0) / 104);
  background: linear-gradient(to top, color-mix(in oklch, currentColor 88%, black), color-mix(in oklch, currentColor 30%, white));
  box-shadow: 0 0 1.8cqmin color-mix(in oklch, currentColor 80%, transparent);
}
tbody tr::after {
  top: calc(0.9cqmin - var(--ring));
  height: 8.5cqmin;
  transform-origin: 50% 0;
  scale: 1 calc(0.04 + attr(data-key type(<number>), 0) / 104);
  background: linear-gradient(color-mix(in oklch, currentColor 45%, transparent), transparent);
}

/* The core: the fourth band's level cell, at the center. */
tbody tr:nth-child(4) td[data-col="level"] {
  display: block;
  position: absolute;
  left: -7cqmin;
  top: -7cqmin;
  width: 14cqmin;
  height: 14cqmin;
  border-radius: 50%;
  font-size: 0;
  background: radial-gradient(circle, #fff 0, oklch(90% 0.08 330) 14%, oklch(66% 0.27 335 / 0.9) 38%, oklch(45% 0.22 300 / 0) 70%);
  box-shadow: 0 0 9cqmin 1cqmin oklch(62% 0.26 330 / 0.35);
  scale: calc(0.62 + var(--level) / 230);
  transition: scale 0.12s ease-out;
}

/* A vignette over everything. */
table::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, transparent 55%, rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55));
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  tbody { animation: none; }
  tbody tr::before, tbody tr::after, td { transition: none; }
}
